Playing Algorithm~\ref{algo:main_algo} with initial phase length $T_1$ time and probability slack $\delta>0$, where
\begin{align*}
    T_1 = C_1 \, \frac{d^2}{\rho_{\min}^2} \log^4(KT/\delta) \log(dT/\delta) \,\,\,\, \text{and}
\end{align*}
\vspace{-2mm}
\begin{align*}
    d \geq C_1 \frac{\log T}{\log \log T} \log (K^2/\delta).
\end{align*} 
Then the regret of the player for a horizon of $T$ satisfies
\begin{align*}
    R(T) &\leq C_2  \left[ \left( \frac{d}{\rho_{\min}} \right)^{3/2} \,\mathsf{\Lambda}^5 \,\, \mathfrak{T} \,\, \sqrt{\log T} \right] \\
